counterfactuals.output:
A portable display stand comprising:

an open-top box structure having a base wall and a plurality of side walls defining an interior compartment and an upper access opening;

a plurality of foldable legs pivotably coupled to the box structure and selectively movable between a deployed position, in which the legs extend from the box structure to support the stand above an underlying surface, and a stowed position adjacent the box structure;

one or more support arms movably coupled to the box structure, each support arm being adjustable between a retracted position and an extended position;

a plurality of panels hingedly connected to at least one of the box structure and the support arms, the panels being movable between a closed configuration and a display configuration; and

a plurality of chambers associated with the panels, the support arms, or the interior compartment, each chamber being configured to removably receive and visibly present at least one safety item.

In the display configuration, the support arms and hinged panels are positionable to arrange the chambers at respective viewing locations. In the closed configuration, the panels cooperate with the box structure to enclose or protect the safety items, and the legs and support arms are foldable or retractable to provide a compact, transportable assembly. The safety items may comprise warning signs, reflective devices, lights, first-aid supplies, fire-suppression equipment, personal protective equipment, traffic-control articles, or combinations thereof.
